# Auto Push Completed Work

## Purpose

Invoke the GitHub push workflow after completed implementation work so the remote repository and connected webapp stay synchronized.

## When This Applies

- Completed features
- Completed fixes
- Completed UI updates
- Completed refactors
- Completed configuration changes

## Required Workflow

1. Read .cursor/project-connections.md when present.
2. Run applicable checks before commit.
3. Review diff and exclude unsafe files.
4. Commit with a clear conventional message.
5. Push to the configured remote and report result.

## Standards

- Push only completed implementation work.
- Do not push planning or review only tasks.
- Let configured GitHub deployment integrations handle webapp deployment.
- Do not manually deploy unless explicitly requested.
- If push fails, diagnose and retry once when safe.

## Do Not

- Do not push partial or broken work.
- Do not push secrets or local config.
- Do not deploy to an unapproved provider.
- Do not treat preview URLs as production.
- Do not invent push success.

